61. Rotate List

https://leetcode.com/problems/rotate-list/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-05-05

Given the head of a linked list, rotate the list to the right by k places.

 
Example 1:
Input: head = [1,2,3,4,5], k = 2
Output: [4,5,1,2,3]

Example 2:
Input: head = [0,1,2], k = 4
Output: [2,0,1]
 

Constraints:

The number of nodes in the list is in the range [0, 500].
-100 <= Node.val <= 100
0 <= k <= 2 * 10^9

APPROACH : SIMPLE SIMULATION AND LITTLE BIT OF MATHS. first checking if k==0 or head is null or ahving 1 node only then return the given head only, 
           after this finding the length of the linked list and then for rotaing to right by k places we will find the postion of the list from front with the 
           formula as length - k ==> will give the position from starting from where we need to shift. 


CODE: 

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* rotateRight(ListNode* head, int k) {

        if(head == NULL || head->next == NULL || k == 0)
            return head;

        // Step 1: Find length
        int length = 0;
        ListNode* temp = head;

        while(temp) {
            length++;
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // Step 2: Optimize k
        k = k % length;
        if(k == 0) return head;

        // Step 3: Find new tail
        int start = length - k;
        temp = head;

        for(int i = 1; i < start; i++) {
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // Step 4: Break and rotate
        ListNode* newhead = temp->next;
        temp->next = NULL;

        // Step 5: Go to end of new list
        ListNode* curr = newhead;
        while(curr->next != NULL) {
            curr = curr->next;
        }

        curr->next = head;

        return newhead;
    }
};
